{
  "$comment": "Anti-AI writing rules, mechanized. Two layers: `base` is the generic tell list — seeded from Wikipedia's 'Signs of AI writing' and a working writer-pack checklist, each rule here because it marks text that reads like nobody in particular wrote it. `site` is this site's house style, filled by the /onboard-marketing skill and edited by hand. scripts/check-voice.mjs enforces both; the /refresh-anti-ai-rules skill updates `base` from its sources via PR (never silently — these rules gate CI). Severity: `banned*` fail the check; `watchWords`, `hedges` and `crutch` are reported as warnings because each has legitimate uses a grep cannot judge. Era-tagged tells rotate: the refresh skill retires stale ones and adds new ones as the sources move.",
